Z||000000||Haze_Performance||04-05-2000||01:10 AM||||Anyone know were I can buy this stuff?  <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/cf.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com/cf.html</A>   .<BR>I went to my auto parts stores and they couldnt help me (Trac Auto, Forest City, Pep Boys and Auto Zone) If someone knows where I can get it PLEASE let me know... I tried to use the link on the page but it dosent work.. Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||04-05-2000||03:30 AM||||I haven't had any luck either, I did a web search for Rally, which is where I found that URL for the article. I emailed them about requesting a catalog or anything, but they didn't bother to reply.. DXR_DAD is the person you should talk to, I don't remember off the top of my head where he bought the CF vinyl. He was kind enough to send me a sample of it (thanks!) and I wouldn't mind getting some for myself! Upon close inspection you can tell it's not CF of course, but it still looks great IMHO. I wouldn't hesitate to use this product.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||04-05-2000||03:34 AM||||Whoa. you weren't kidding about that link not working.. it's not even the same site anymore!<P>when I put that article up, it was the company page for the people who made the CF vinyl.. now it looks like it's not.. DXR_DAD.. if that product is still available where you bought it.. you might want to stock up on what they have left, looks like the company might not be around anymore..||||reg||1
